Package: lifewatt
Title: Environmental Justice Indicators by US State and ZCTA
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Your", "Name", , "you@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides environmental justice indicators at the granularity each
    source publishes: state-level residential electricity prices (observed
    EIA-861 annual and EIA-861M monthly series, with a validated forecast beyond
    the observed window) and their year-over-year and month-over-month trends,
    bill-based price evidence, an expected life-expectancy loss view anchored to
    published national life tables (with any life-expectancy translation
    declared as a sensitivity parameter until a sourced elasticity exists), and
    a synthetic life-expectancy estimate built from state mortality rates whose
    assumptions are declared in the output; plus ZCTA-level adult health
    estimates from the CDC PLACES 2025 release (crude prevalence with 95%
    confidence limits for the 2023 BRFSS measures). No realised average
    residential price is published per ZIP code, so a ZIP is resolved to its
    state with 'zip_to_state()' rather than priced directly.
